      "body": "In commit \"rpc: handle malformed jsonrpc 2.0 requests correctly\" (02380237ddd2ed6878d7a3b0ae2807cfcf2cd9ff)\n\nInstead of adding a third place that converts a caught error into a reply (with the [batch loop](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/02380237ddd2ed6878d7a3b0ae2807cfcf2cd9ff/src/httprpc.cpp#L172-L179) and the outer catch), it could be simpler to make [`JSONErrorReply()`](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/02380237ddd2ed6878d7a3b0ae2807cfcf2cd9ff/src/httprpc.cpp#L41-L46) do the right thing for 2.0 requests, replacing the `Assume` with the behavior it asserts. Then this `parse()` call can stay as it was, and any error thrown after the version is known gets the 2.0 treatment, not just parse errors. Diff from master:\n\n```diff\n--- a/src/httprpc.cpp\n+++ b/src/httprpc.cpp\n@@ -40,10 +40,17 @@ static bool g_rpc_whitelist_default = false;\n\n static UniValue JSONErrorReply(UniValue objError, const JSONRPCRequest& jreq, HTTPStatusCode& nStatus)\n {\n-    // HTTP errors should never be returned if JSON-RPC v2 was requested. This\n-    // function should only be called when a v1 request fails or when a request\n-    // cannot be parsed, so the version is unknown.\n-    Assume(jreq.m_json_version != JSONRPCVersion::V2);\n+    // A request known to be JSON-RPC 2.0 gets the error in the reply with HTTP\n+    // success, or no reply if it is a notification. HTTP error statuses are\n+    // only returned for 1.x requests and requests whose version is unknown.\n+    if (jreq.m_json_version == JSONRPCVersion::V2) {\n+        if (jreq.IsNotification()) {\n+            nStatus = HTTP_NO_CONTENT;\n+            return {};\n+        }\n+        nStatus = HTTP_OK;\n+        return JSONRPCReplyObj(NullUniValue, std::move(objError), jreq.id, jreq.m_json_version);\n+    }\n\n     // Send error reply from json-rpc error object\n     nStatus = HTTP_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR;\n```\n\nThis would also help #36753, which currently builds the 2.0 reply for a whitelist denial itself and could just throw the error for both versions.\n\nI tested this diff together with the PR's test changes: `interface_rpc.py`, including the new tests, and `rpc_whitelist.py` pass in a debug build.",
