      "body": "In commit \"rpc: handle malformed jsonrpc 2.0 requests correctly\" (02380237ddd2ed6878d7a3b0ae2807cfcf2cd9ff)\n\nNot a blocker, but if we want to comply with the spec it seems like this case should get an error reply instead of 204. The JSON-RPC 2.0 spec's [examples](https://www.jsonrpc.org/specification#examples) answer an invalid Request object with no id (`{\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"method\": 1, \"params\": \"bar\"}`) with an error and `\"id\": null`, treating it as an invalid request rather than a notification. If we don't want to comply with the spec, the test comment should be updated to say this is intentional. The [test comment suggestion](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36758#discussion_r4472774752) includes that.\n\nNote that compatibility with previous bitcoin core releases shouldn't be a concern in this case since before this PR this request made debug builds abort on the `Assume` in `JSONErrorReply()`, and release builds returned HTTP 400 with a \"Missing method\" error and no id.",
