      "body": "In commit \"rpc: handle malformed jsonrpc 2.0 requests correctly\" (02380237ddd2ed6878d7a3b0ae2807cfcf2cd9ff)\r\n\r\nnit: The [JSON-RPC 1.1 vs 2.0 table](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/6355c9f8cf64b8c41a85ead6ca20fb2e88bd4ecf/doc/JSON-RPC-interface.md?plain=1#L92) says 2.0 requests get HTTP 200 \"unless there is an actual HTTP server error (request parsing error, endpoint not found, etc)\", which could be read as covering the malformed requests tested here. Probably makes sense to update that documentation to say \"request body is not valid JSON\" instead, to match the behavior after this PR.",
